    "magnitude": "mean |score_male - score_female| on each model's own output scale (its CrossEncoder default: scores in (0, 1) for BGE and Jina, unbounded logits for MiniLM). Both runs score a given model on the same scale (see score_range), so each ratio compares like with like; ratios are not comparable to raw score gaps across models",
    "flips": "top-3 membership from the exact-k ranks; net_female_form = female-form-only minus male-form-only. The binomial p tests female_form_only ~ Binomial(n_flips, 1/2) and is descriptive only: the 3,840 comparisons come from 192 pools of 20 focal comparisons that share their other members, and 1,952 distinct résumés fill them, so flips are not independent",
    "by_construction": "prepended = mode inject: a frequency-matched male or female given name, with one surname shared by both forms, prepended and any pronouns made to agree with it; swap_in_window / swap_truncated = mode swap with marker_in_token_window true / false. Every prepended comparison has its marker in the window, so prepended plus swap_in_window are the in-window comparisons and swap_truncated the outside-window ties. n_prepended_document_carried_a_name counts prepended comparisons whose document carried a detected given name that swapping could not change, so that name stays in both forms. ratio_synthetic_to_companion is the model's synthetic mean |score_male - score_female| over the group's (null when the group's is 0). Shares, gaps and flips are defined as above"
